  "notes": "CONJUGATION (ichidan):\n- Negative: {真似|まね}ない\n- Te-form: {真似|まね}て\n- Past: {真似|まね}た\n- Potential: {真似|まね}られる\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive. Takes を for the thing being imitated.\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {真似|まね} (noun): imitation, mimicry\n- {真似|まね}をする: to imitate (noun + する construction, more common in casual speech)\n- {物真似|ものまね}: impersonation, mimicry (as entertainment)\n\nUSAGE:\n{真似|まね}る can be neutral (learning through imitation) or negative (copying without originality). Context determines the nuance. The noun + する form {真似|まね}をする is often more natural in everyday conversation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {動|うご}きを{真似|まね}る: to copy movements\n- {声|こえ}を{真似|まね}る: to mimic a voice\n- {人|ひと}の{真似|まね}をする: to imitate someone",
